Interactive render delegate edits of a shader imager graph through a UsdImagingGL.Engine, from python

A red sphere is rendered with the imager graph of an ArnoldNodeGraph, set by the arnold:global:imager render setting.
The exposure of its root imager is edited, before and during the render, an imager_color_correct is inserted after it
and removed, the root imager is replaced by an imager_shader whose flat shader is edited during the render, and the
imager setting is cleared. Covers the fixes of the imager updates (#2758, #2764). The render delegate is driven by a
headless UsdImagingGL.Engine as a viewport does, see testsuite/common/interactive_engine_test.py. Each render is
checked in test.py, and the last one is compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet
are reported as warnings (known issues in test.py).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'script': '"{}" test.py'.format(usd_python)}
